<edge source="russia_ukraine_war_diplo::information_flow" target="eurozone_bond_stress::sovereign_bond_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge in rapid, actionable information about military escalation or sanctions triggers faster market repricing of tail‑risk exposure, pushing up yields on eurozone sovereign bonds as investors demand higher compensation.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war_diplo</data>
  <data key="d39">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war_diplo::information_flow" target="turkey_regional_realignm::drone_attack_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher volumes and speed of operational intelligence and targeting data exchanged around the Russia–Ukraine war enable state and proxy operators to mount more frequent and precise unmanned-aerial strikes in adjacent theatres, raising regional drone incident rates.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war_diplo</data>
  <data key="d39">turkey_regional_realignm</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war_diplo::information_flow" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::investor_sentiment_index" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Release or leakage of actionable intelligence about cyber operations, illicit tech transfers, or vulnerability exposures tied to the conflict raises perceived operational and sanction risk for AI-exposed firms, directly depressing investor confidence in AI assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war_diplo</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
