<edge source="russia_ukraine_war_diplo::regulatory_response" target="eurozone_bond_stress::fiscal_financing_pressur" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger legal and sanctioning measures that restrict access to financial markets and counterparties increase borrowing costs and limit rollover options for affected governments, raising short‑to‑medium‑term fiscal financing pressure.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war_diplo</data>
  <data key="d39">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war_diplo::regulatory_response" target="turkey_regional_realignm::energy_supply_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Broader legal and sanctions measures tied to diplomacy over the war disrupt trade channels and contractual certainty for energy suppliers and shippers linked to the region, increasing the probability of pipeline/LNG or shipping interruptions affecting Turkey's energy flows.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war_diplo</data>
  <data key="d39">turkey_regional_realignm</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war_diplo::regulatory_response" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::chip_rare_earth_supply" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Rapid expansion of sanctions and export controls tied to the Russia–Ukraine conflict directly restricts suppliers and exports of advanced semiconductor equipment and certain critical materials, reducing immediate hardware availability for AI supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war_diplo</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war_diplo::regulatory_response" target="us_china_tech_rivalry::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter FDI screening, licensing requirements, and sanctions introduced in response to war-related security concerns raise compliance costs and legal risk for cross-border investments into AI firms (notably into China-linked entities), reducing capital flows into those AI assets.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war_diplo</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
