<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::chip_rare_earth_supply" target="eurozone_bond_stress::sovereign_bond_yields" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A material tightening of advanced semiconductor or rare‑earth supply increases input costs and forces catch‑up investment and supply‑chain retooling in eurozone industry, boosting inflation expectations and risk premia and thereby putting upward pressure on long‑term sovereign yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">eurozone_bond_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::chip_rare_earth_supply" target="mid_east_gulf_escalation::diplomatic_deescalation" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Restricted access to critical chips and rare earths (driven by tech competition) prompts affected powers to intensify state‑level outreach and bargain with Gulf suppliers and intermediaries, increasing coordinated diplomatic engagement aimed at stabilizing ties.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">mid_east_gulf_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::chip_rare_earth_supply" target="russia_ukraine_war_diplo::private_comm_control" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved availability of advanced semiconductors and critical materials enables private firms and platform providers to expand and harden communications infrastructure (e.g., edge devices, satellites), increasing private-sector control over communications used in and around the conflict.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war_diplo</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_tech_rivalry::chip_rare_earth_supply" target="turkey_regional_realignm::maritime_control_cap" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Export controls and supply disruptions to advanced chips and critical materials reduce Turkey's ability to procure and produce naval sensors, maritime radars, unmanned surface/underwater vehicles and communications gear, degrading its effective maritime monitoring and interdiction capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">turkey_regional_realignm</data>
</edge>
